\section{Comparison of runs}
The geometry was unchanged between runs A and B.  Applying Eq.~\eqref{eq:rth-def} to each record gives
\begin{equation}\label{eq:probe-ratio}
\frac{R_{\mathrm{th},A}}{R_{\mathrm{th},B}}=\frac{(T_{h,A}-T_{c,A})/\dot Q_A}{(T_{h,B}-T_{c,B})/\dot Q_B}.
\end{equation}
Contact losses were subtracted before forming the temperature differences.

