\section{Recorded discussion}
The estimator time constant $\tau_e=18\,\mathrm{ms}$ suppresses sensor noise.  The actuator time constant $\tau_a=42\,\mathrm{ms}$ limits the attainable bandwidth.  This time constant was fixed during the robustness sweep, while the gain was varied by $\pm20\%$.  The minutes do not record whether the estimator or actuator parameter was meant.

% engineBlind
\section{Reduced population model}
We replaced the conductance kernel by its mean whenever within-bin fluctuations were negligible.  This approximation reduces the convolution to $I(t)=\bar g\,s(t)$.  The retained recordings provide bin means but no variances or error bounds, so the degree to which the approximation applies to the reported bursts cannot be established.

